+
+### Two things that must line up
+
+1. **The chain-id key must match your target network.** The app is "live on
+   Base," so the key is `8453` (Base mainnet). `useScaffoldReadContract` looks up
+   by `scaffold.config.ts` → `targetNetworks[0].id`. If you're actually running
+   dev against Base Sepolia (`84532`) or local Hardhat (`31337`), the `8453`
+   entry won't be found and you'll get the same silent `undefined`. Register
+   under whatever chain id you're pointing at (or add entries for each).
+
+   - Native USDC on Base mainnet (8453): `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`
+   - USDC on Base Sepolia (84532): `0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e`
+   - (Note: `0xd9aAEc86B65D86f6A7B5B1b0c42FFA531710b6CA` is the *bridged* USDbC —
+     a different token. Use the native address above unless you specifically want
+     USDbC.)
+
+2. **Keep `as const`.** Scaffold-ETH's type inference for
+   `useScaffoldReadContract` (autocompleting `functionName: "balanceOf"` and
+   typing `args`/return) depends on the ABI being a readonly literal. Dropping
+   `as const` doesn't break runtime but kills the type safety.
+
+USDC has **6 decimals**, so format the returned `uint256` with `6`, not `18`
+(e.g. `formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6)`).
+
+---
+
+## Summary of the arc
+
+| Stage | What happened | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Original bug | `usdcBalance` `undefined`, no error, no request | USDC unregistered → hook can't resolve name → `query.enabled = false` → wagmi never calls |
+| Teammate's "fix" | Pasted USDC into `deployedContracts.ts`, worked all week | Registry now had USDC; no deploy ran to disturb it |
+| Regression | `yarn deploy` blanked the page again | `deployedContracts.ts` is generated from Hardhat deployments and rewritten on deploy; USDC isn't deployed by the project, so it was dropped |
+| Correct fix | Put USDC in `externalContracts.ts` under chain id `8453` with an ERC-20 ABI, `as const` | Hand-maintained file, merged into the registry, never overwritten by deploy |

